{
  "level": "Year 7",
  "subject": "selective",
  "title": "What quantitative reasoning tests",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "What QR is",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Quantitative reasoning, or QR, gives you numbers, shapes or tables.",
          "write": "QR = find the rule"
        },
        {
          "say": "You're not tested on how much maths you remember.",
          "write": "not memorised facts"
        },
        {
          "say": "You're tested on finding a pattern, checking it and using it.",
          "write": "find • check • use"
        },
        {
          "say": "It's multiple choice. Only one option is correct.",
          "write": "4 or 5 options, 1 correct"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The question types",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "There are six shapes of question.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Six QR question types",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 30,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "Sequences"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 30,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "Grids"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 110,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "Symbol puzzles"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 110,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "purple",
                "label": "Comparing amounts"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 190,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "Shape patterns"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 190,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "pink",
                "label": "Tables and graphs"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "A sequence: 3, 7, 11, 15. Add 4 each time.",
          "write": "3, 7, 11, 15, 19"
        },
        {
          "say": "Symbol puzzles: triangle plus triangle is 10, so triangle is 5.",
          "write": "▲ + ▲ = 10 → ▲ = 5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Comparing: is 20 percent of 50 bigger than 50 percent of 20?",
          "write": "20% of 50 vs 50% of 20"
        },
        {
          "say": "They're equal. Both are 10.",
          "write": "10 = 10"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Spot, test, choose",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Spot the type first. Naming it tells you which tools to use.",
          "write": "1. Spot"
        },
        {
          "say": "Find a rule from the first part. 7 minus 3 is 4.",
          "write": "2. Rule: add 4",
          "draw": {
            "type": "numberline",
            "from": 0,
            "to": 24,
            "start": 3,
            "jump": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Test it on every part. 11, 15 and 19 all go up by 4.",
          "write": "3. Test: +4 +4 +4 ✓"
        },
        {
          "say": "Now choose. 19 plus 4 is 23.",
          "write": "4. Choose: 23",
          "draw": {
            "type": "numberline",
            "from": 0,
            "to": 24,
            "start": 19,
            "jump": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Work it out before you look at the options.",
          "write": "answer first, options second"
        },
        {
          "say": "Doubling 19 gives 38. But doubling doesn't turn 3 into 7.",
          "write": "✗ 38"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "A number grid",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Here's a grid. Find the rule across the rows.",
          "write": "Find ?",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Three by three grid with a missing number",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
